findings.problem:
While hovering is true, a waiting step has no time limit. Only a hover exit or onDisappear saves it, and neither runs when the app terminates. Before FD a step was lost only if the app quit within 0.8 s of the last click (the FB review accepted that). Now it is lost if the app quits at any time while the pointer still rests on the row. The quit paths that do not move the pointer:
- a remote quit, `pixelswitch quit` or MCP (AppController.swift:204);
- a Sparkle relaunch (AutoUpdatePolicy.mayInstallNow checks switching and sign-in, not a waiting step);
- logout or restart;
- probably Cmd-Q in the Settings window.
While the step waits, the row shows a number that auto-switch, the menus, the widget and the CLI do not use. Hover can also stay true with no exit event: when a re-sort from another row's save, a CLI/MCP write or a trackpad scroll moves the row out from under a still pointer, or when the app deactivates. In those cases the keyboard pause stays off until the next real exit or disappear, so the save is delayed rather than lost unless the app quits. A keyboard user whose pointer happens to rest on the row is in the same position. That last part cannot be confirmed without running the app.
